      "rationale": "Flush mux was embedded between the two synchronizer stages (w0→sync_wrptr and f0→sync_flush), creating a long clk-to-q + mux + setup inter-stage path. By moving the mux to a combinational wire before the first stage register, the inter-stage critical path is reduced to a single register setup time only. Gate count unchanged (mux moved, not duplicated). Functional equivalence: flush resets both stages to zero in both implementations with identical 2-cycle latency.",
